---
/**
 * Privacy policy (CalOPPA). Plain English and limited to what the site really does:
 * contact form → Web3Forms → Proofpoint spam filter → Microsoft 365 (GoDaddy) sales inbox;
 * hCaptcha bot check on form step 2; Vercel hosting logs; OpenFreeMap map tiles;
 * no analytics or ads, no cookies set by the site itself (checked in the code 2026-10-29,
 * wording updated 2026-11-05). Armak should review the wording.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/pages/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const effective = 'November 5, 2026';
const description = `How ${site.name} handles the information you send through armak.tech, including the contact form. No ads, no tracking, and your details are never sold.`;
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description={description}>
  <PageHero
    label="Privacy"
    title="Privacy policy."
    lead={`What ${site.name} collects through this website, why, and what you can ask us to do with it. Effective ${effective}.`}
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}
  />

  <article class="privacy container">
    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Through the contact form, we collect only what you choose to send us: your name, company (optional), email
        address, phone number, the kind of project you have in mind and your message.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form also passes along what kind of request it is (a site assessment, a quick question or a service
        request) and, if you opened it from a link on this site such as a glossary term, the topic of that link.
      </p>
      <p>
        Like nearly every website, the servers that host this site keep standard technical logs, such as your IP
        address, browser type and the pages you visit.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">How we use it</h2>
      <p>
        We use what you send us to reply to you, schedule a site assessment, answer your question or service request,
        and scope your project. We don’t use it for anything else, and we don’t sell it, rent it or share it with
        anyone for marketing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep the emails the contact form sends us as business records.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">Who else handles it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Web3Forms</strong> delivers the contact form to our inbox ({site.email}) by email. Your browser sends
          the form to them directly, so they receive what you typed and your IP address. Their own privacy policy
          covers what they do with it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>hCaptcha</strong> checks that the contact form is sent by a person. It loads only when you reach the second step of the form, where you enter your details and message.
          When it loads, it receives your IP address and standard browser details, and it may store data in your
          browser for its own check. Their own privacy policy covers what they do with it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email.</strong> The email carrying your form details first passes through a spam filter run by
          Proofpoint. It is then stored in our Microsoft 365 mailbox, which we buy through GoDaddy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Vercel</strong> hosts this website and keeps the standard server logs described above.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OpenFreeMap</strong> supplies the service-area map. When the map loads, your browser requests map
          data from their servers, so they receive your IP address and standard browser details.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>We don’t load anything else on this site from outside companies.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">Cookies and tracking</h2>
      <p>
        This site doesn’t set cookies, and it has no advertising, analytics or tracking tools. It doesn’t follow you
        across other websites, and no other company runs ads or tracking here. Because of that, we don’t change
        anything when your browser sends a “Do Not Track” signal.
      </p>
      <p>
        There is one exception. The hCaptcha check on the contact form may store data in your browser while it runs.
        It is not used for advertising, and nothing else on this site does this.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask for a copy of the information you’ve sent us, or ask us to correct it. Email
        <a href={site.emailHref}>{site.email}</a> or call <a href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phone}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">Children</h2>
      <p>This website is for businesses and isn’t directed at children under 13.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="t-h3">Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If we change this policy, we’ll post the new version on this page with a new effective date.
        This version is effective {effective}.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
    padding-block: 1rem var(--space-section);
  }

  .privacy section {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.875rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .privacy p,
  .privacy li {
    color: var(--steel);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .privacy strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .privacy ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.625rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .privacy a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .privacy a:hover {
    color: var(--signal);
  }
</style>
